# Time Precision & Early Preview Implementation

We have successfully hardened the audio pipeline and unleashed the GPU on translations. Now, we are addressing your requests for better time tracking and the ability to "preview" the dub before the 15-hour lipsync process.

## Proposed Changes

### [MODIFY] [main_ui.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it2/app/main_ui.py)
**Objective**: Update time formatting to `DD:HH:MM:SS`.
- Rewrite `format_time` to calculate days, hours, minutes, and seconds.
- Update the status table logic to ensure the "ETR" (Estimated Time Remaining) also uses this high-precision format.

### [MODIFY] [main_ui.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it2/app/main_ui.py)
**Objective**: "Selective Preview" Iteration.
- Add **Start Point (s)** and **Duration (s)** input boxes/sliders.
- Upgrade the Test button to **"🎬 Preview Selection"**.
- Feature: This will automatically slice your favorite scene and run it *only* through the translation and audio mix stages.

### [MODIFY] [pipeline.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it2/app/pipeline.py)
**Objective**: Early Mux & Selective Stopping.
- **Auto-Preview**: Every job will now generate a `preview_dub.mp4` immediately after the audio mix.
- **Selective Stop**: If the job is a "Preview Selection" task, the pipeline will stop after Phase 5, giving you the result in seconds instead of hours.

### [MODIFY] [main_ui.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it2/app/main_ui.py)
**Objective**: Time Precision.
- Re-write the timer to `DD:HH:MM:SS` format for both Elapsed and ETR.

## User Review Required
> [!NOTE]
> The early preview will have the correct voice and timing, but the original Chinese mouth movements will still be visible (as lipsync hasn't run yet). 
> 
> Does this approach meet your needs for a mid-tier quality check?
